{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And her father had spit, etc.</b> The verse clothed the measure of the matter in this language, and did not say 'if the father spits in the face of his daughter,' etc., to tell that she is in the category of a daughter, which is the level of the righteous." "And it doubled to say <b>spit, spit</b>, to say that if one had cried out to Him beforehand He would not have spat in her face, and this is the measure of the matter: <b>and her father spit</b> — meaning, when she caused that he spat in her face and there was no one who could persuade him not to spit until he spat. And His saying <b>spit</b> a second time, etc. — from this you learn that if there had been a manner in which Moses would have prayed beforehand, she would not have been punished." "<b>She shall be shut up seven days.</b> It appears that the tzara'at had already departed from her through Moses' prayer, as per His saying ״רְפָא נָא״ — meaning, now; only that HaShem decreed that she sit as one ostracized, for if not, the verse would not have needed to say ״תִּסָּגֵר״ — it is obvious that she would be shut up until she was healed of her tzara'at. Rather, certainly she had already been healed, and therefore too the verse did not mention the purification of her tzara'at on the day of her gathering. And according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Zevaḥim 102a; Sifrei) that Aaron did not see Miriam's tzara'at on account of closeness, it is explained correctly, for since there is no tzara'at here — for there is no priest to declare impure — if so, there is here nothing but seclusion alone, as one ostracized. Or it is possible that she was secluded by decree of HaShem our Elohim, who is a priest, and His saying <b>she shall be shut up</b>, etc. — here is the seclusion; and she was purified by decree of HaShem, as it is written <b>and afterward she may be gathered.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:16.996101899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}